@*
===========================================================
ORANGE TENDER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
PAGE: Purchase Request Review / Approval

DEVELOPER OWNER: Doulat
MODULE: Department / Purchase Requests (Sourcing Officer review step)
TRELLO TASK: Purchase Request Review / Approval
TRELLO URL: https://trello.com/c/cOYVH9co

PURPOSE:
The Sourcing Officer reviews a submitted request and
accepts, returns or rejects it.

BUSINESS ACCESS:
Sourcing Officer (business user). Doulat is the developer;
the requesting department cannot use this page.

ROUTE: /SourcingOfficer/PurchaseRequests/Review/{id?}

FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION:
- Load the request with Items and Reviews (Status must be
  Submitted).
- POST Accept / Return / Reject: update the current
  PurchaseRequestReview (Decision, Comment,
  ReviewedByUserId, ReviewedAt) and PurchaseRequest.Status.
- Notify the requesting user and write AuditLogs.

DEPENDENCIES:
PurchaseRequests, PurchaseRequestItems,
PurchaseRequestReviews, Notifications, AuditLogs.

STATUS:
UI SCAFFOLD ONLY — BUSINESS LOGIC NOT IMPLEMENTED.

IMPORTANT:
No separate department approval stage. Only the Sourcing
Officer decides here.
===========================================================
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Purchase Request Review / Approval";
    ViewData["WorkspaceSection"] = "Requests";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Review a submitted purchase request: accept it for tendering, return it for correction, or reject it.";
}
<partial name="_PageHeader" />
<partial name="_ScaffoldNotice" />

<section class="ws-panel pg-panel">
    <h2>Request</h2>
    <dl class="pg-dl">
        <div><dt>Reference</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Title</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Department</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Requested by</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Priority</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Needed by</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Submission #</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Submitted</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
    </dl>
</section>

<section class="ws-panel pg-panel" aria-labelledby="tbl-requested-items">
    <div class="pg-panel-head"><h2 id="tbl-requested-items">Requested items</h2></div>
    <div class="pg-table-wrap">
        <table class="pg-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item / service</th><th scope="col">Specifications</th><th scope="col">Quantity</th><th scope="col">Unit</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody><tr><td colspan="4"><partial name="_EmptyState" model='"No items loaded."' /></td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ws-panel pg-panel" aria-labelledby="tbl-earlier-submissions">
    <div class="pg-panel-head"><h2 id="tbl-earlier-submissions">Earlier submissions</h2></div>
    <div class="pg-table-wrap">
        <table class="pg-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Submission #</th><th scope="col">Submitted</th><th scope="col">Decision</th><th scope="col">Comment</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody><tr><td colspan="4"><partial name="_EmptyState" model='"This is the first submission."' /></td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="pg-grid">
<partial name="_ConfirmAction" model='new ConfirmActionModel("Accept request", "Accept the request so a tender can be created from it.", "Sets the request to Accepted and records the decision on the current PurchaseRequestReview.", false, false)' />
<partial name="_ConfirmAction" model='new ConfirmActionModel("Return for correction", "Send the request back to the department with what must be fixed.", "Sets the request to Returned. The department can edit and resubmit; this submission stays in history.", true, false)' />
</div>

<partial name="_ConfirmAction" model='new ConfirmActionModel("Reject request", "Reject the request entirely.", "Sets the request to Rejected with your reason.", true, true)' />

<nav class="pg-links" aria-label="Related pages">
    <ul>
        <li><a asp-area="" asp-controller="Clarifications" asp-action="Index">Ask the department for clarification</a></li>
        <li><a asp-area="SourcingOfficer" asp-controller="PurchaseRequests" asp-action="Index">Back to requests</a></li>
    </ul>
</nav>
